//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// MummyTKT's Bias Pointer v6 — BACKTEST EDITION (on-chart labels)
//
// The live alert script plus labels: wherever the live script sends a bias
// alert, this one puts an "H4 aligned - Alert" label on that H4 candle,
// filtered the way Alert Filters filter Telegram (defaults = defaults):
//   Origin (BUY / SELL CONFIRMED)   External on, Internal off
//   H4 back in line                 External on, Internal off
//   H4 breakout in line, Breaker Origin / retest, OC reaction, Engulfing (wick)
// Continuations follow the setup's latest H4 confirmation (External / Internal).
//
// BEING TRIED OUT HERE FIRST (not in the live alerts yet):
//   • Daily V-shapes (A-shapes for sells) formed after the Daily breakout,
//     beyond the Daily Breaker, are reaction levels while the direction holds
//     (they die on a Daily close through them, like every Daily level).
//   • A fresh Daily reaction followed by an H4 breakout alerts EVERY time,
//     also while H4 is still aligned after the Origin:
//     "Daily reaction + H4 breakout". Each fresh reaction after a confirmation
//     starts its own External / Internal check.
//   • A new Daily breakout in the SAME direction doesn't reset H4: in-line
//     breakouts and H4 reactions keep firing. A reaction at the new breakout's
//     Daily levels + an H4 breakout then becomes what H4 rides on. Only a Daily
//     breakout the other way resets H4.
//
// The label sits on the candle that CLOSED to confirm: entry = next candle's open.
// Daily data is read from completed candles only, so history doesn't repaint.
// No alert needs to be created on this copy.
//
//
// Apply to a 4H chart for each instrument.
// Create ONE alert per instrument: condition = "Any alert() function call"
//                                   webhook  = https://forex-radar.fly.dev/api/tv-webhook
//
// Event types:
//   BREAKOUT         — Daily candle closed beyond the most recent external
//                      high/low (level_type "external")
//   RETEST           — H4 entered a reaction source zone
//   RETEST_CANCELLED — H4 moved away from zone without H4 confirmation
//   CONFIRMED        — H4 closed beyond an H4 A/V level during a daily retest (Origin)
//   INVALIDATED      — no longer sent: a break the other way is a new BREAKOUT
//   H4_CONTINUATION  — H4 continuation event after Origin has fired
//                      cont_type: breakout_cont | inline_break | breaker_origin | breaker_cont | oc_cont | engulfing
//   PRICE_UPDATE     — Current H4 close price, powers dashboard price-level alerts
//
// v5 change: added PRICE_UPDATE event — fires at every realtime H4 close.
// 2026-10-16: every completed post-breakout daily OC is watched (not just the
//             latest) until an opposing breakout; a daily-zone reaction stays
//             valid on later candles — any later H4 close beyond the H4 A/V
//             confirms it — and only fails on an H4 close back through the zone.
//            Backend uses it to check subscriber price-level alerts.
// 2026-10-16 (b): daily candles read with lookahead_on (history no longer a day
//             late after a paste); pip sizes match the server's table; every
//             webhook carries "timeframe"; PRICE_UPDATE carries a chart snapshot
//             (stage + all levels); "moved away first" can't be inherited from
//             the previous breakout; External/Internal is judged against the
//             CURRENT reaction's start (also after a failed reaction restarts).
// 2026-10-18: daily bias comes from market structure — external, internal and
//             inner internal highs/lows (wick levels, body-close breaks, no
//             tolerance). The most recent break on any layer is the breakout;
//             its level is the breaker and the rest of that range is the
//             inside-range zone. D.A/D.V are wick levels and only the one in line
//             with the bias is shown (D.V for buys, D.A for sells).
// 2026-10-19: retest and H4-aligned chart markers removed. Layers replaced by
//             ONE most-recent external high/low: structures form inside the
//             current range at any depth (same rules) and only the newest pair
//             is drawn; its latest break is the daily breakout.
//             H4 Breaker / H4 OC continuations only count a candle that OPENS on
//             the bias side of the level (a climb through it from below — or a
//             drop through it from above for sells — is not a rejection).
//             Reactions must touch the level exactly (no ±tolerance on the
//             touch). H4 is out of line on a close beyond the LATEST H4 V (buy)
//             / A (sell); that drops every H4 OC until H4 breaks back in line,
//             and an H4 OC closed through against the bias is dropped.
//             Inside-range reactions must come from a Daily V-shape (A-shape for
//             sells) or Daily OC level inside the broken range: exact touch, hold;
//             the reaction fails on a close through that level.
//             H4 out of line → H4 only realigns after a FRESH daily reaction
//             (same three zones), then an H4 break; the alert names that level.
//             External/Internal is judged from the first reaction at the daily
//             level that confirms (a failed reaction restarting there keeps it).
//             H4 OCs: every OC of the latest H4 breakout leg (and after it) is
//             watched; each alerts once on a rejection then is removed; checked
//             before a new candle can form the next OC; all dropped when H4
//             breaks the other way or on a new daily breakout.
//             Daily levels (structure, D.A/D.V, inside-range V/A) come from
//             candle BODIES by default; setting "Daily levels from" = Wick
//             restores the wick levels.
//             Daily reaction levels (V/A-shapes, Daily OCs, post-breakout OCs)
//             die once a Daily candle closes through them; dead levels never
//             count as a reaction again.
//             While H4 is in line, every new H4 close beyond the latest H4 A
//             (buy) / V (sell) alerts ("H4 breakout in line with the Daily"); its
//             level becomes the H4 Breaker and its leg's OCs are kept.
//             Webhooks carry the exchange (syminfo.prefix); on Deriv synthetic
//             indices and crypto one pip is 0.002% of price (5-pip allowance = 0.01%).
//             PRICE_UPDATE carries the closed H4 candle and the last Daily candle;
//             each new alert first sends 40 Daily then 40 H4 candles (HISTORY)
//             for the server's chart pictures.
//             Weekly storyline: Weekly External breakout → Weekly reaction (on
//             Daily candles) → Daily breakout in the Weekly direction is
//             Weekly-confirmed (Internal / External); bias alerts carry wk_* fields.
//             H4 engulfing (body covers the previous opposite body; eng_wick when it
//             also closes beyond that candle's wick) after the
//             Origin, in line, in the Daily direction: cont_type "engulfing".
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

indicator("MummyTKT Bias Pointer — Backtest", overlay=true, max_bars_back=2000, max_lines_count=100, max_labels_count=500)

// ── Backtest labels (same switches as Alert Filters) ──────────────────────────
GBT = "Backtest labels"
bool   bt_weekly   = input.bool(false, "Weekly (lines, labels, Weekly AGAINST marks)", group=GBT,
     tooltip="Off: Daily + H4 only. The Weekly never changes which alerts fire; it only adds context.")
bool   bt_ext      = input.bool(true,  "External H4 breakouts", group=GBT)
bool   bt_int      = input.bool(false, "Internal H4 breakouts", group=GBT)
bool   bt_origin   = input.bool(true,  "Origin — BUY / SELL CONFIRMED", group=GBT)
bool   bt_react    = input.bool(true,  "Daily reaction + H4 breakout (after the Origin)", group=GBT)
bool   bt_realign  = input.bool(true,  "H4 back in line", group=GBT)
bool   bt_inline   = input.bool(true,  "H4 breakout in line", group=GBT)
bool   bt_breaker  = input.bool(true,  "H4 Breaker (Origin + retests)", group=GBT)
bool   bt_oc       = input.bool(true,  "H4 OC reaction", group=GBT)
bool   bt_engulf   = input.bool(true,  "H4 engulfing", group=GBT)
string bt_eng_mode = input.string("Wick", "Engulfing covers", options=["Wick", "Body only", "Both"], group=GBT)
int    bt_from     = input.time(timestamp("2020-01-01T00:00:00"), "Backtest from", group=GBT,
     tooltip="Labels and counts start at this date. Earlier candles still build the levels.")
bool   bt_latest   = input.bool(true,  "Keep only the latest alert label (clean chart)", group=GBT,
     tooltip="Each new alert label deletes the previous one. The count table still counts every alert. Switch off to see the whole history.")
bool   bt_grey     = input.bool(true,  "Show alerts that are not counted (grey, with the reason)", group=GBT,
     tooltip="Alerts before the start date, Internal ones while Internal is off, and types switched off above.")
bool   bt_table    = input.bool(true,  "Show count table", group=GBT)
bool   bt_lvls     = input.bool(true,  "Show the Daily reaction levels being watched (4H)", group=GBT,
     tooltip="Every Daily level the script would accept a reaction at right now. A level that is missing here can't trigger an alert.")
color  bt_buy_col  = input.color(#00C853, "Buy label", group=GBT, inline="btc")
color  bt_sell_col = input.color(#FF1744, "Sell label", group=GBT, inline="btc")
// counts: 0 Origin, 1 Back in line, 2 In line, 3 Breaker Origin, 4 Breaker retest, 5 OC, 6 Engulfing,
//         7 Daily reaction + H4 breakout, 8 Buys, 9 Sells
var bt_cnt  = array.new_int(10, 0)
var int bt_t0 = time
// External / Internal of the setup's latest H4 confirmation (Origin, Daily reaction
// + H4 breakout, or back in line); continuations follow it, like the server
var bt_scls = array.from("")
var bt_last = array.new<label>(1, na)   // the alert label currently on the chart
// The External H4 level of the current Daily reaction: the latest H4 A (buys) /
// V (sells) when the reaction started, i.e. formed BEFORE it
var float bt_ext_a = na
var float bt_ext_v = na
var BT_NAMES = array.from("Origin", "Back in line", "H4 breakout in line", "Breaker Origin", "Breaker retest", "OC reaction", "Engulfing", "Daily reaction + H4 breakout")

// ── Inputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
